      <div type="prooemium" n="III">
        <head>Liber III, prooemium: III 1–93</head>
        <argument>
          <p>Traditio textus (vv. 1–621): Ω (= O Γ [= Q V]). The text of this section rests upon the consensus of the Carolingian archetype Ω, witnessed by O and the Γ-branch (Q and V). Critical text follows Deufert (2019).</p>
        </argument>
        <lg type="poem">
          <!-- III 1 -->
          <l xml:id="III1" n="1">
            <app type="critical">
              <lem wit="#Omega"><w lemma="o">O</w></lem>
              <rdg wit="#alpha-A" type="conjecture"><w lemma="e">E</w></rdg>
              <rdg resp="#SH" type="conjecture"><w lemma="tu">Te</w></rdg>
              <note>O Ω, defend. Wakefield, Timpanaro (1960) : E α-A : Te Shackle (1921) 156</note>
            </app>
            <w lemma="tenebra">tenebris</w>
            <w lemma="tantus">tantis</w>
            <w lemma="tam">tam</w>
            <w lemma="clarus">clarum</w>
            <w lemma="extollo">extollere</w>
